.Trashes

# IDE
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
# Everything under .vscode is local except the one setting the repository has
# an opinion about, so the directory is excluded by its contents rather than by
# itself: git does not descend into an excluded directory, and a negation
# inside one never matches.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json

# Claude
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Go
vendor/
bin/
dist/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.test
*.prof

# Built binaries, if someone builds in place rather than into bin/
/spacebar

# Local credentials and state. Nothing under here is ever committed.
#
# The OAuth token and the webhook URL live in the OS keyring, or, when there is
# no keyring, under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME at mode 0600. Never in the repository and
# never in the config file (SPEC.md §5.3). These patterns are the second line:
# a webhook URL is a bearer credential in a query string, and one pasted into a
# scratch file is one `git add .` from being public.
*.pem
*.key
.netrc
# Anchored to the root on purpose. Unanchored, these would also match
# internal/config/testdata/config.json, and a fixture that git silently refuses
# to track is a test that passes locally and fails for everybody else.
/config.json
/credentials.json
